message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "UK Packaging Recovery Evidence, 2023 to 2026: What the published data shows, and what it cannot"
abstract: >-
  An analysis of seven public UK datasets covering packaging producer
  responsibility: recovery evidence (PRN and PERN), the register of obligated
  producers, placed-on-market returns under the packaging Extended Producer
  Responsibility regulations, and evidence revenue. Each dataset was prepared
  from its raw published files with explicit cleaning rules and a validation
  log. Four findings are reported: that half of evidenced recycling is
  discharged by export and that the split by material tracks the price of
  evidence rather than any policy instrument; that agreed protocols mean a
  credited tonne can represent as little as 0.6 per cent packaging content;
  that the share of evidence issued after the compliance year has closed rose
  from 9.6 to 14.5 per cent in three years; and that published totals rest on
  returns that were outstanding at publication, concentrated in Q4 and in
  plastic export.
